## 1. Project Model

This project follows a **source-available and community-driven development model** with a separate commercial Cloud Edition. The source is public and contributions are welcome, but this is deliberately **not an OSI-approved open-source license**: the commercial restrictions in Section 5 go beyond what that definition permits.

The **Community Core** is publicly available and intended to be freely used, inspected, modified, forked, and improved by the community. Contributions from the community are welcome and are an important part of the project's development.

The **Cloud Edition** is a separate commercial offering operated by Igor Dlugosh. It provides hosted and managed functionality and may include additional proprietary features, infrastructure, services, and support.

The Software may be used for personal purposes as well as for internal commercial purposes. Organizations may deploy and use the Software within their own businesses without requiring a commercial license.

However, the Software may not be commercially redistributed, resold, white-labeled, or offered as a third-party hosted service without prior written permission from Igor Dlugosh.

The purpose of this model is to keep the core technology open and community-driven while allowing the project owner to maintain and commercially operate the official Cloud Edition.

