## 4. Internal Commercial Use

Commercial use of the Software is permitted when the Software is used as an internal tool or component of your own business activities.

For example, an organization may deploy the Software on its own infrastructure and use it to:

* operate internal business processes;
* support its employees;
* develop its own products;
* provide its own services;
* manage its own operations; or
* otherwise conduct its own commercial activities.

The fact that an organization generates revenue through its business does not, by itself, constitute a violation of this License.

The restriction applies to **commercializing the Software itself**, rather than using the Software as part of your own business.

---

## 5. Commercial Restrictions

Without prior written permission from Igor Dlugosh, you may not:

### 5.1 Sell or Resell the Software

Sell, license, rent, lease, sublicense, or otherwise commercially distribute the Software or a Modified Version as a standalone product.

### 5.2 Offer the Software as a Hosted Service

Operate the Software or a Modified Version as a commercial SaaS, PaaS, hosted application, managed service, or similar service for third parties.

### 5.3 Create a Competing Commercial Product

Use the Software or a Modified Version as the basis for a commercially offered product or service that substantially competes with the Cloud Edition.

### 5.4 White-Label or Rebrand the Software

Repackage, white-label, rebrand, or otherwise present the Software or a Modified Version as your own commercial software product.

### 5.5 Commercially Redistribute Modified Versions

Commercially distribute a Modified Version where the primary value or functionality being sold is provided by the Software.

Requests for written permission may be sent to `hello@veilio.dev`.

---

## 6. Cloud Edition

The Cloud Edition is the official commercial hosted offering of the project.

The Cloud Edition may be provided through paid subscriptions and may include:

* managed hosting;
* automatic updates;
* backups;
* infrastructure and scalability;
* monitoring;
* enterprise functionality;
* technical support;
* proprietary features;
* other hosted or managed services.

The Community Core and Cloud Edition may share common code, concepts, or functionality. However, access to the Community Core does not grant any right to commercially operate a competing hosted version of the Cloud Edition.

The Cloud Edition may be governed by separate Terms of Service, subscription agreements, privacy policies, and commercial licenses.

